:"code","id":"changelog_prune_dangling_edges","label":"prune_dangling_edges()","rationale":"Removes edges whose source or target is not in the node set","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.10","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_export_py","label":"export.py","rationale":null,"source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.10","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_serve_py","label":"serve.py (MCP stdio server)","rationale":"call_tool() wraps dispatch in try/except so handler exceptions return error strings instead of crashing the stdio loop (#163)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_validate_graph_path","label":"validate_graph_path()","rationale":"Circular containment check replaced with an existence + .json suffix check so graphs outside cwd load without a security hole","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.3.26","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_norm_label","label":"norm_label field","rationale":"Written at build time for diacritic-insensitive search with Unicode NFKD normalization fallback (#293)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.10","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_cache","label":"SHA256 semantic/AST cache","rationale":"Namespaced into cache/ast/ and cache/semantic/ with flat entries read as migration fallback; file_hash() uses the path relative to project root so entries are portable across machines and CI runners (#311)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.5.3","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_report_py","label":"report.py","rationale":"Skips the file-stats section when passed a warning key, because cluster-only runs skip detection and leave the stats dict empty (#422)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.21","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_god_nodes","label":"god_nodes()","rationale":"Field renamed from edges to degree for clarity (#375)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.15","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_suggest_questions","label":"suggest_questions()","rationale":"Uses k=100 approximate betweenness sampling above 1000 nodes and returns early above 5000 nodes to bound runtime (#341)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.14","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_surprising_connections","label":"surprising_connections()","rationale":null,"source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.3","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_cluster_py","label":"cluster.py","rationale":"cluster() converts directed graphs to undirected internally because Leiden requires an undirected graph (#125)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_louvain_fallback","label":"Louvain fallback","rationale":"max_level=10 and threshold=1e-4 prevent indefinite hangs on large sparse graphs while preserving community quality (#48)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.3.11","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_hooks_py","label":"hooks.py","rationale":"Hooks use #!/bin/sh not #!/bin/bash because Git for Windows ships sh.exe; shebang allowlist validation prevents metacharacter injection (#140)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_pretooluse_hook","label":"PreToolUse hook","rationale":"Matches on Bash instead of Glob|Grep for Claude Code v2.1.117+; emits systemMessage at top level to satisfy codex-cli's additionalProperties:false schema (#138)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.5.2","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_tree_sitter","label":"tree-sitter AST backend","rationale":"Pinned >=0.23.0 with a version guard because stale bindings produced silent empty AST output or cryptic TypeErrors (#89, #52)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.3.20","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_raw_calls","label":"raw_calls cross-file resolution post-pass","rationale":"Unresolved callees are saved per file and resolved against a global label map in a post-pass, extending cross-file call edges beyond Python to ~all supported languages (#298, #348)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.19","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_go_pkg_prefix","label":"go_pkg_ import node prefix","rationale":"Go stdlib imports are prefixed with the full import path so they stop colliding with local files of the same basename and creating false cycle-dependency pairs (#431)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.23","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_graphify_install","label":"graphify install","rationale":"Refreshes .graphify_version in every known skill directory so stale-version warnings clear across all previously installed platforms (#178)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.23","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_graphify_query","label":"graphify query","rationale":"BFS/DFS traversal of graph.json so the graph is queryable without the Claude Code skill","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.3.8","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_graphify_update","label":"graphify update","rationale":"Exits with code 1 on rebuild failure instead of silently returning; prunes ghost nodes from deleted files before merging (#287, #51)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.14","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_graphify_clone","label":"graphify clone <github-url>","rationale":null,"source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.5.0","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_graphify_merge_graphs","label":"graphify merge-graphs","rationale":"Combines multiple graph.json outputs into one cross-repo graph","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.5.0","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"document","id":"changelog_skill_md","label":"skill.md pipeline","rationale":"Step B2 requires subagent_type=general-purpose because the read-only Explore type silently dropped extraction results (#195)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_html_renderer","label":"vis.js HTML renderer","rationale":"Replaced pyvis with a custom renderer; labels/file types/community names HTML-escaped before innerHTML injection to close XSS","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.1.4","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"changelog_obsidian_export","label":"Obsidian vault export","rationale":"GRAPH_REPORT.md links to community hub files so the vault stays in one connected component (#221)","source_file":"CHANGELOG.md","source_location":"0.4.2","source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_graphify","label":"graphify","rationale":"Maps a project into a knowledge graph you query instead of grepping; not a vector index — a real graph you traverse, with no embeddings or vector store","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":"https://graphify.com"},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_graph_json","label":"graph.json","rationale":null,"source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_graph_html","label":"graph.html","rationale":null,"source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_graph_report","label":"GRAPH_REPORT.md","rationale":null,"source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_confidence_tags","label":"EXTRACTED / INFERRED confidence tags","rationale":"Every edge is tagged so users can tell what was read directly from the source apart from what graphify resolved","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_tree_sitter_local","label":"local tree-sitter AST parsing","rationale":"Code is parsed deterministically with no LLM so nothing leaves the machine; only the semantic pass over docs/media calls a backend","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_semantic_pass","label":"semantic pass over docs/PDFs/images/video","rationale":null,"source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_god_nodes","label":"god nodes","rationale":"The most-connected concepts, showing what everything flows through","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_communities","label":"Leiden communities","rationale":"Splits the graph into subsystems with LLM-free labels","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"readme_graphify_query","label":"graphify query","rationale":"Returns a scoped subgraph for a plain-language question","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"readme_graphify_path","label":"graphify path A B","rationale":null,"source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"readme_graphify_explain","label":"graphify explain","rationale":null,"source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"code","id":"readme_graphify_install","label":"graphify install","rationale":null,"source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_strict_mode","label":"strict mode (--strict / GRAPHIFY_HOOK_STRICT)","rationale":"Blocks the first raw source read of a session and redirects it to the graph, then reverts to the soft nudge so it fires at most once and never gets stuck","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_project_install","label":"--project scoped install","rationale":"Writes the skill under the current repo instead of the user profile so it can be committed","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_platform_matrix","label":"multi-platform assistant support","rationale":"Trae has no PreToolUse hook support, so AGENTS.md is its always-on mechanism; OpenClaw and Aider use sequential extraction because parallel agent support is still early there","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_optional_extras","label":"optional install extras","rationale":"Split per feature so users install only what they need; leiden is gated to Python < 3.13","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_graphifyy_package","label":"graphifyy PyPI package","rationale":"Official package is graphifyy (double-y) while the CLI command stays graphify; other graphify* packages are unaffiliated. uv tool/pipx installs are preferred over pip because the skill resolves Python from graphify-out/.graphify_python and a mismatched env yields ModuleNotFoundError","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_benchmarks","label":"LOCOMO / LongMemEval benchmarks","rationale":"All systems ran on the same harness, model and budgets, scored by a judge blind-validated against a second judge (90.6% agreement, Cohen's kappa 0.81)","source_file":"README.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null},{"author":null,"captured_at":null,"contributor":null,"file_type":"concept","id":"readme_mcp_server","label":"MCP stdio server","ra